 Re: r-cran-xml2: autopkgtest failure against libxml2 2.9.10
In-Reply-To: <4225c3d3-4822-cd9c-acaf-0c210db4b8b9@gmail.com>
References: <20200227182006.GA3348783@mapreri.org>
 <20200227182006.GA3348783@mapreri.org>
 <4225c3d3-4822-cd9c-acaf-0c210db4b8b9@gmail.com>
 <20200227182006.GA3348783@mapreri.org>
Message-ID: <20200305150251.GU3348783@mapreri.org>

Hi,

On Tue, Mar 03, 2020 at 04:22:47PM +0100, Michael R. Crusoe wrote:
> At https://salsa.debian.org/r-pkg-team/r-cran-xml2/-/commit/e973a8d9500dc3a98e34dcd5eb7e86cf5b692bb6
> I've commited a fix for this bug.
> 
> 
> If a DD could sponsor that upload or grant me upload rights, I would
> appreciate it.

I see Dylan uploaded it.
However, that's not enough, now you are effectively requiring xml 2.9.10
for that test, so you need to require that version in both build-deps
and test-deps.  Else, the version of libxml2 currently in testing is
enough to satisfy the dependency, and the test fails the opposite way it
was doing before.

-- 
regards,
