Dear maintainers,

r-cran-gwidgets and r-cran-gwidgetstcltk are new in Debian. However the
autopkgtest of r-cran-gwidgets shows that you probably have a typo (dot
instead of hyphen) in the versioned Depends of your package.

Broken r-cran-gwidgetstcltk:amd64 Depends on r-cran-gwidgets:amd64 <
0.0-54.1-2 @ii pmK > (>= 0.0.51)

This can also be seen on your migration QA page:
https://qa.debian.org/excuses.php?package=r-cran-gwidgetstcltk

r-cran-gwidgetstcltk/amd64 has unsatisfiable dependency
r-cran-gwidgetstcltk/i386 has unsatisfiable dependency
Rejected due to piuparts regression -
https://piuparts.debian.org/sid/source/r/r-cran-gwidgetstcltk.html

Please fix your Depends.

Paul

