Subject: [R-pkg-team] Bug#954913: ITP: r-cran-rcdklibs -- the CDK libraries
 packaged for GNU R
Message-ID: <158512468752.3641959.1309922572245210428.reportbug@energija.fam-tille.de>

Package: wnpp
Severity: wishlist

Subject: ITP: r-cran-rcdklibs -- the CDK libraries packaged for GNU R
Package: wnpp
Owner: Andreas Tille <tille at debian.org>
Severity: wishlist

* Package name    : r-cran-rcdklibs
  Version         : 2.3
  Upstream Author : Rajarshi Guha,
* URL             : https://cran.r-project.org/package=rcdklibs
* License         : LGPL-2
  Programming Lang: GNU R
  Description     : the CDK libraries packaged for GNU R
 An R interface to the Chemistry Development Kit, a Java library for
 chemoinformatics. Given the size of the library itself, this package is
 not expected to change very frequently. To make use of the CDK within R,
 it is suggested that you use the 'rcdk' package. Note that it is
 possible to directly interact with the CDK using 'rJava'. However 'rcdk'
 exposes functionality in a more idiomatic way. The CDK library itself is
 released as LGPL and the sources can be obtained from
 <https://github.com/cdk/cdk>.

Remark: This package is maintained by Debian R Packages Maintainers at
   https://salsa.debian.org/r-pkg-team/r-cran-rcdklibs


